  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual material via deictic pronouns",
  "description": "The meme's text contains the deictic pronouns 'i' and 'you', which directly address the viewer/user. The user is projected onto the textual material (text_chunk_1) as the implied recipient of the message. The text 'i could have killed all of them. but i let some of them survive so you know why i killed them.' uses 'i' to attribute the action to Hitler (as visually projected) and 'you' to address the viewer, making the user the target of the hateful justification. This creates a direct semiotic projection where the user is positioned as the one being addressed by the fictionalized narrative.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
